     sseennddmmaaiill — a mail enqueuer for smtpd(8)

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     sseennddmmaaiill [--ttvv] [--FF _n_a_m_e] [--ff _f_r_o_m] _t_o _._._.

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The sseennddmmaaiill utility is a local enqueuer for the smtpd(8) daemon, compat‐
     ible with mailwrapper(8).  The message is read on standard input (stdin)
     until sseennddmmaaiill encounters an end-of-file.  The sseennddmmaaiill enqueuer is not
     intended to be used directly to send mail, but rather via a frontend
     known as a mail user agent.

     Unless the optional --tt flag is specified, one or more recipients must be
     specified on the command line.

     The options are as follows:

     --FF _n_a_m_e
             Set the sender's full name.

     --ff _f_r_o_m
             Set the sender's address.

     --tt      Read the message's To:, Cc:, and Bcc: fields for recipients.  The
             Bcc: field will be deleted before sending.

     --vv      Enable verbose output.

     To maintain compatibility with Sendmail, Inc.'s implementation of
     sseennddmmaaiill, various other flags are accepted, but have no effect.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The sseennddmmaaiill utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

